Michael G. Kurilla (mgk2r@Virginia.EDU) wrote:
: Having recently ascended with a Valk for the first time, I'm
: wondering if when I try it again I need to be as concerned with
: AC as I was before.  I have seen people posting ascensions with
: ACs of -14 or such.  I put alot of effort into getting my AC
: down to -27 without priestly donations.  Various attempts to
: get a reduction from donation resulted in a measly extra point
: to -28.

: My question is how valuable is this?  Exactly how does the AC
: affect the ability of monsters to hit and do damage?  Is there
: a point of diminishing returns?  Damage from enchanted weapons
: just seems to go up; does armor protection work the same way?
: Can one become invincible?  What is the lowest AC for monsters?

AC of >0 starts to reduce the amount of damage a hit does
i.e. if you have -10 and a hit was going to take 8, 
the hit is a miss.

The lowest AC I've ever had was -48, 

A couple of games ago I was accending with an AC -47 and
got surronded by dragons on the air level. I decided to 
keep my RoC off and see if I could take them all out.
Well my 300+ hp character got down to about 60 hp
and he was using Grayswandir to beat on the dragons. So,
NO YOU CANNOT BECOME INVINCIBLE!!! BTW I put my RoC on
and recoverd all my hit points.

